Forgive my pendanticism, but I believe the worse case scenario for
generating scrolls of charging from a magic marker is 4 scrolls,
rather than 5 (or 3, as in my earlier incorrect assessment.) Writing a
scroll of charging consumes between 8 and 15 charges. Minimum charges
in a randomly generated marker are (0:30). So, assuming all attempts
consume the maximum of 15 ink, you can write two scrolls, use one of
those to recharge the marker to (1:50), then write 3 more scrolls,
leaving your marker at (1:5). So you end up with 1+3 =3D 4 scrolls of
charging.

Your point about avoiding the exageration of the 'best case scenario'
is excellent, however. A player's ascension ratio typical sky-rockets
as soon as they learn to pay more heed to the 'worst case scenario'.
Fountain quaffing is an excellent early-game example.


